($q$GATE-OS-1999-Q05$q$, $q$GATE-OS-1999-Q05$q$, 1999, 3, $q$Deadlocks$q$, $q$Deadlock Free Resource Condition$q$, 5, 'NAT', $q$A system has 4 processes sharing N instances of a single resource type. If each process requires at most 3 instances of the resource, what is the minimum value of N to guarantee that deadlock will never occur?$q$, $q${}$q$::jsonb, $q$9$q$, $q$To guarantee a system with m processes each needing up to k resources is deadlock-free, the minimum total resources N must satisfy:
N >= m * (k - 1) + 1
Here m = 4 processes, max requirement k = 3.
N >= 4 * (3 - 1) + 1 = 4 * 2 + 1 = 9 resources.$q$, $q$1. Worst-Case Allocation: Give each process 1 resource less than its maximum requirement (k - 1 = 2 resources).
2. Total resources held in worst case = m * (k - 1) = 4 * 2 = 8 resources.
3. At this point, all 4 processes are waiting for 1 more resource (system is at brink of deadlock).
4. Adding 1 extra resource (+1) allows at least one process to complete and release all its resources.
5. Minimum N = 8 + 1 = 9.$q$, $q${}$q$::jsonb, ARRAY[$q$Deadlock Avoidance$q$,$q$Pigeonhole Principle$q$,$q$Resource Calculation$q$]::text[], ARRAY[$q$N_min = sum(Max_i - 1) + 1$q$]::text[], ARRAY[$q$Multiply (processes) by (max_demand - 1) and add 1.$q$]::text[], 'Easy', $q$Forgetting to add 1 at the end, getting 8 instead of 9.$q$, $q$Resource Allocation 1989-2000 | L 19$q$, 'Verified', $q$[]$q$::jsonb),
($q$GATE-OS-2007-Q31$q$, $q$GATE-OS-2007-Q31$q$, 2007, 3, $q$Deadlocks$q$, $q$Banker's Algorithm Safety Trace$q$, 31, 'MCQ', $q$Consider a system with 5 processes (P0-P4) and 3 resource types (A, B, C). Current Allocation and Max demand matrices are given. Available vector is (3, 3, 2). Which of the following safe sequences exists?$q$, $q${"A":"<P1, P3, P4, P0, P2>","B":"<P0, P1, P2, P3, P4>","C":"<P2, P1, P3, P4, P0>","D":"No safe sequence exists"}$q$::jsonb, $q$A$q$, $q$Banker's Safety Algorithm calculates Need = Max - Allocation. Starting with Available=(3,3,2), P1's Need (1,2,2) <= Available (3,3,2). P1 executes and releases allocation, increasing Available. Continuing this produces safe sequence <P1, P3, P4, P0, P2>.$q$, $q$1. Calculate Need Matrix: Need[i] = Max[i] - Allocation[i].
2. Compare Need[P1] = (1, 2, 2) <= Available (3, 3, 2) -> True.
3. P1 finishes: New Available = Available + Allocation[P1] = (3,3,2) + (2,0,0) = (5,3,2).
4. Compare Need[P3] = (0, 1, 1) <= (5, 3, 2) -> True. P3 finishes: New Available = (5,3,2) + (2,1,1) = (7,4,3).
5. P4 finishes -> P0 finishes -> P2 finishes.
6. Safe Sequence: <P1, P3, P4, P0, P2>.$q$, $q${"A":"Valid safe sequence.","B":"Fails at P0 because Need[P0] > Initial Available.","C":"Fails at P2 initially.","D":"Safe sequence exists."}$q$::jsonb, ARRAY[$q$Banker's Algorithm$q$,$q$Safe State$q$,$q$Resource Allocation$q$]::text[], ARRAY[$q$Need[i] = Max[i] - Allocation[i]$q$,$q$Available_new = Available_old + Allocation[i]$q$]::text[], ARRAY[$q$Always update Available by ADDING finished process Allocation.$q$]::text[], 'Medium', $q$Subtracting Need from Available instead of adding Allocation upon process completion.$q$, $q$Resource Allocation 2001-2009 | L 20$q$, 'Verified', $q$[{"code":"MISSING_DATA","severity":"error","message":"Allocation and Max matrices are not included in the question text."}]$q$::jsonb),
($q$GATE-OS-2002-Q03__deadlocks$q$, $q$GATE-OS-2002-Q03$q$, 2002, 3, $q$Deadlocks$q$, $q$Resource Allocation Graph & Deadlock$q$, 3, 'MCQ', $q$A Resource Allocation Graph (RAG) contains 5 processes and 4 resource types with 1 instance each. If there is a cycle in the RAG, does deadlock necessarily exist?$q$, $q${"A":"Yes, always","B":"No, never","C":"Yes, because single instance per resource type","D":"Insufficient information"}$q$::jsonb, $q$C$q$, $q$In a Resource Allocation Graph where every resource type has EXACTLY ONE instance, a cycle is a necessary AND sufficient condition for deadlock.$q$, $q$1. Single Instance Resource: Cycle == Deadlock.
2. Multi Instance Resource: Cycle is necessary but NOT sufficient for deadlock.
3. Since graph specifies 1 instance each, cycle strictly guarantees deadlock.$q$, $q${"A":"Only true for single instance resources.","B":"Incorrect.","C":"Correct due to single instance specification.","D":"Single instance guarantees sufficiency."}$q$::jsonb, ARRAY[$q$Resource Allocation Graph$q$,$q$Deadlock Cycle$q$,$q$Single Instance Resource$q$]::text[], ARRAY[$q$Cycle in Single-Instance RAG <=> Deadlock$q$]::text[], ARRAY[$q$For single instance resources, cycle directly implies deadlock.$q$]::text[], 'Easy', $q$Confusing single-instance and multi-instance RAG properties.$q$, $q$Resource Allocation 2009-2021 | L 21$q$, 'Verified', $q$[{"code":"DUPLICATE_ID","severity":"warning","message":"Original id GATE-OS-2002-Q03 is used by 2 different questions; this one was re-keyed as GATE-OS-2002-Q03__deadlocks. Original kept in source_id."},{"code":"TEMPLATE_FAMILY","severity":"info","message":"One of several questions with near-identical wording in this dataset (only numbers, year or format differ)."}]$q$::jsonb),
