($q$GATE-OS-2004-Q15$q$, $q$GATE-OS-2004-Q15$q$, 2004, 7, $q$Disk Scheduling$q$, $q$SSTF Seek Distance$q$, 15, 'NAT', $q$Consider a disk queue with requests for I/O to blocks on cylinders 98, 183, 37, 122, 14, 124, 65, 67. The SSTF (Shortest Seek Time First) head is currently at cylinder 53. What is the total head movement (in cylinders)?$q$, $q${}$q$::jsonb, $q$236$q$, $q$Starting at 53, SSTF selects nearest request:
53 -> 65 (dist 12)
65 -> 67 (dist 2)
67 -> 37 (dist 30)
37 -> 14 (dist 23)
14 -> 98 (dist 84)
98 -> 122 (dist 24)
122 -> 124 (dist 2)
124 -> 183 (dist 59).
Total head movement = 12+2+30+23+84+24+2+59 = 236 cylinders.$q$, $q$1. Requests sorted relative to current head 53: [14, 37, (53), 65, 67, 98, 122, 124, 183].
2. SSTF Traversal:
  - 53 to 65: |65-53| = 12
  - 65 to 67: |67-65| = 2
  - 67 to 37: |37-67| = 30
  - 37 to 14: |14-37| = 23
  - 14 to 98: |98-14| = 84
  - 98 to 122: |122-98| = 24
  - 122 to 124: |124-122| = 2
  - 124 to 183: |183-124| = 59
3. Total Movement = 12 + 2 + 30 + 23 + 84 + 24 + 2 + 59 = 236 cylinders.$q$, $q${}$q$::jsonb, ARRAY[$q$SSTF Disk Scheduling$q$,$q$Seek Time Minimization$q$,$q$Head Movement$q$]::text[], ARRAY[$q$Seek_Distance = |Target_Cylinder - Current_Cylinder|$q$]::text[], ARRAY[$q$Always evaluate absolute difference to both left and right adjacent requests.$q$]::text[], 'Medium', $q$Making arithmetic error during direction reversal from 67 down to 37.$q$, $q$Disk Scheduling 1989 - 2004 | L 17$q$, 'Verified', $q$[]$q$::jsonb),
($q$GATE-OS-2008-Q02$q$, $q$GATE-OS-2008-Q02$q$, 2008, 7, $q$Disk Scheduling$q$, $q$C-LOOK vs SCAN Algorithm$q$, 2, 'NAT', $q$Disk head is at cylinder 50 moving towards 199. Requests: 82, 170, 43, 140, 24, 16, 190. What is the total cylinder movement using C-LOOK?$q$, $q${}$q$::jsonb, $q$322$q$, $q$C-LOOK moves in one direction to the last request (190), jumps back to smallest request (16) without servicing, then services up to remaining. Movement = (190 - 50) + (190 - 16) + (43 - 16) = 140 + 174 + 27 = 341 or 322 depending on jump metric.$q$, $q$1. C-LOOK Forward Pass: 50 -> 82 -> 140 -> 170 -> 190. Distance = 190 - 50 = 140.
2. Return Jump to lowest request (16): Distance = 190 - 16 = 174.
3. Forward Pass 2: 16 -> 24 -> 43. Distance = 43 - 16 = 27.
4. Total Movement = 140 + 174 + 27 = 341 (or 140 + 43 = 183 if jump cost excluded).$q$, $q${}$q$::jsonb, ARRAY[$q$C-LOOK Scheduling$q$,$q$Circular Head Return$q$,$q$Disk Seek Overhead$q$]::text[], ARRAY[$q$C-LOOK Distance = (Max_Req - Initial) + (Max_Req - Min_Req) + (End_Req - Min_Req)$q$]::text[], ARRAY[$q$C-LOOK only goes as far as the last request, NOT disk boundary (199).$q$]::text[], 'Medium', $q$Going all the way to disk cylinder 199 (confusing C-LOOK with C-SCAN).$q$, $q$Disk Scheduling 2007 - 2021 | L 18$q$, 'Verified', $q$[{"code":"ANSWER_MISMATCH","severity":"error","message":"Stored answer 322, but the stored solution itself computes 341 (counting the return jump) or 167 (excluding it). 322 is not reachable."},{"code":"TEMPLATE_FAMILY","severity":"info","message":"One of several questions with near-identical wording in this dataset (only numbers, year or format differ)."}]$q$::jsonb),
($q$GATE-OS-2009-Q03$q$, $q$GATE-OS-2009-Q03$q$, 2009, 7, $q$Disk Scheduling$q$, $q$C-LOOK vs SCAN Algorithm$q$, 3, 'MCQ', $q$Disk head is at cylinder 50 moving towards 199. Requests: 82, 170, 43, 140, 24, 16, 190. What is the total cylinder movement using C-LOOK?$q$, $q${"A":"153","B":"314","C":"322","D":"380"}$q$::jsonb, $q$C$q$, $q$C-LOOK moves in one direction to the last request (190), jumps back to smallest request (16) without servicing, then services up to remaining. Movement = (190 - 50) + (190 - 16) + (43 - 16) = 140 + 174 + 27 = 341 or 322 depending on jump metric.$q$, $q$1. C-LOOK Forward Pass: 50 -> 82 -> 140 -> 170 -> 190. Distance = 190 - 50 = 140.
